<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Koskari &mdash; a Lisp that lives with Python</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Koskari is a stackless Lisp for Python: first-class continuations, ambient async, and an indentation layout that reads blocks into forms.">
  <meta property="og:title" content="Koskari">
  <meta property="og:description" content="A Lisp that lives with Python. First-class continuations, ambient async, indentation layout.">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">

  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wght@12..96,500;12..96,600;12..96,700;12..96,800&family=Hanken+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="koskari-icon.svg">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>

<body>
<div class="ko-page">

  <!-- nav -->
  <div class="ko-nav">
    <div class="ko-brand">
      <img src="koskari-icon.svg" alt="" width="34" height="34">
      <span class="ko-brand-name">Koskari</span>
      <span class="ko-version">v{{ version }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ko-nav-links">
      <a class="ko-link" href="/docs/">Docs</a>
      <a class="ko-link" href="#examples">Examples</a>
      <a class="ko-link" href="#download">Download</a>
      <a class="ko-link" href="{{ github_url }}">GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- hero -->
  <div class="ko-hero">
    <div>
      <div class="ko-eyebrow">the fourth iteration of the sibilant idea</div>
      <h1 class="ko-h1">A Lisp that lives<br><span class="ko-accent">with Python.</span></h1>
      <p class="ko-lede">Koskari is a stackless Lisp running inside CPython: first-class continuations, ambient async, and an indentation layout that reads blocks into forms. It is built as a playground, with Python's whole ecosystem in reach and fewer of Python's restrictions.</p>
      <div class="ko-cta-row">
        <a class="ko-btn ko-btn-primary" href="/docs/start/overview/">Get started <span class="ko-btn-arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
        <a class="ko-btn ko-btn-secondary" href="/docs/">Browse the docs</a>
      </div>
      <div class="ko-install">
        <span class="ko-install-cmd"><span class="ko-prompt">$</span> pip install --pre koskari</span>
        <span class="ko-install-soon">WEEKLY DEV SNAPSHOTS</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ko-hero-art">
      <div class="ko-hero-mark">
        <img src="koskari-icon.svg" alt="Koskari" width="190" height="190">
      </div>
      <div class="ko-etymology">&#954;&#945;&#955;&#955;&#953;&#963;&#964;&#953;</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- features -->
  <div class="ko-section">
    <div class="ko-label">What it is</div>
    <div class="ko-features-grid">
      <div class="ko-card">
        <div class="ko-card-icon">&#8646;</div>
        <h3 class="ko-card-title">Lives with Python</h3>
        <p class="ko-card-body">Koskari code runs on its own stackless bytecode evaluator inside the CPython process. Import any Python module, subclass its classes, pass objects both ways.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ko-card">
        <div class="ko-card-icon ko-card-icon-sm">(&nbsp;)</div>
        <h3 class="ko-card-title">Layout syntax</h3>
        <p class="ko-card-body">An indentation layout reads blocks into forms at parse time, so most code sits closer to Python than to classic S-expressions. Parenthesized forms mix in freely.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ko-card">
        <div class="ko-card-icon">&#8635;</div>
        <h3 class="ko-card-title">First-class continuations</h3>
        <p class="ko-card-body">The stackless evaluator supports delimited and full continuations, multi-shot included, along with coroutines, tail calls, and dynamic wind.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ko-card">
        <div class="ko-card-icon">&#8767;</div>
        <h3 class="ko-card-title">Ambiently async</h3>
        <p class="ko-card-body">Awaitable values are awaited in place. Any function can suspend and none carries an async marker, so the same code serves synchronous and asynchronous callers.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- example -->
  <div id="examples" class="ko-section ko-section-tight">
    <div class="ko-label ko-label-tight">An example</div>
    <h2 class="ko-section-title">A point, and its neighbors</h2>
    <p class="ko-section-lede">The <span class="ko-inline-code">@dataclass</span> decorator comes straight from Python's standard library. The class body is layout syntax; the parenthesized forms inside it are ordinary S-expressions.</p>
    <div class="ko-code-window">
      <div class="ko-code-chrome">
        <span class="ko-dot ko-dot-close"></span>
        <span class="ko-dot ko-dot-min"></span>
        <span class="ko-dot ko-dot-max"></span>
        <span class="ko-code-filename">point.ki</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ko-code-body">
<pre class="ko-code-pre"><span class="k-kw">import-from</span> dataclasses dataclass
<span class="k-kw">import-from</span> itertools product


<span class="k-kw">define</span> <span class="k-fn">around</span> <span class="k-pn">[</span>i <span class="k-param">reach:</span> <span class="k-num">1</span><span class="k-pn">]:</span>
    <span class="k-pn">(</span><span class="k-fn">range</span> <span class="k-pn">(</span><span class="k-fn">-</span> i reach<span class="k-pn">)</span> <span class="k-pn">(</span><span class="k-fn">+</span> i reach <span class="k-num">1</span><span class="k-pn">))</span>

<span class="k-dec">@dataclass</span>
<span class="k-kw">define-class</span> <span class="k-type">Point</span> <span class="k-pn">[]:</span>
    <span class="k-str">""" A point in 2D space """</span>

    <span class="k-kw">define</span> x <span class="k-pn">::</span> <span class="k-type">int</span> <span class="k-num">0</span>
    <span class="k-kw">define</span> y <span class="k-pn">::</span> <span class="k-type">int</span> <span class="k-num">0</span>

    <span class="k-kw">define</span> <span class="k-fn">neighbors</span> <span class="k-pn">[</span>self <span class="k-param">reach:</span> <span class="k-num">1</span><span class="k-pn">]:</span>
        <span class="k-kw">each</span> <span class="k-pn">[[</span>x y<span class="k-pn">]</span> <span class="k-pn">(</span><span class="k-fn">product</span> <span class="k-pn">(</span><span class="k-fn">around</span> self.x reach<span class="k-pn">)</span> <span class="k-pn">(</span><span class="k-fn">around</span> self.y reach<span class="k-pn">))]:</span>
            <span class="k-pn">(</span><span class="k-type">Point</span> x y<span class="k-pn">)</span>

    <span class="k-kw">define</span> <span class="k-fn">move</span> <span class="k-pn">[</span>self <span class="k-param">x:</span> <span class="k-num">0</span> <span class="k-param">y:</span> <span class="k-num">0</span><span class="k-pn">]:</span>
        <span class="k-pn">(</span><span class="k-fn">incr!</span> self.x x<span class="k-pn">)</span>
        <span class="k-pn">(</span><span class="k-fn">incr!</span> self.y y<span class="k-pn">)</span>

    <span class="k-dec">@property</span>
    <span class="k-kw">define</span> <span class="k-fn">coord</span> <span class="k-pn">[</span>self<span class="k-pn">]:</span>
        <span class="k-pn">#(</span>self.x self.y<span class="k-pn">)</span>

    <span class="k-dec">@coord.setter</span>
    <span class="k-kw">define</span> <span class="k-fn">coord</span> <span class="k-pn">[</span>self value<span class="k-pn">]:</span>
        <span class="k-kw">define-values</span> <span class="k-pn">[</span>x y<span class="k-pn">]</span> value
        <span class="k-pn">(</span><span class="k-fn">set!</span> self.x x<span class="k-pn">)</span>
        <span class="k-pn">(</span><span class="k-fn">set!</span> self.y y<span class="k-pn">)</span></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- docs levels -->
  <div class="ko-section ko-section-tight">
    <div class="ko-label ko-label-tight">Documentation</div>
    <h2 class="ko-section-title ko-section-title-spaced">Find your level</h2>
    <div class="ko-doc-list">
      {% for row in doc_rows %}
      <a class="ko-doc" href="{{ row.href }}">
        <span class="ko-doc-num">{{ row.num }}</span>
        <span class="ko-doc-title">{{ row.title }}</span>
        <span class="ko-doc-blurb">{{ row.blurb }}</span>
        <span class="ko-arrow">&rarr;</span>
      </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- download band -->
  <div id="download" class="ko-download">
    <div class="ko-download-grid">
      <div>
        <h2 class="ko-download-title">Get Koskari</h2>
        <p class="ko-download-lede">Koskari is in early development. Weekly snapshots of <strong class="ko-download-strong">v{{ version }}</strong> publish to PyPI as dev releases; <strong class="ko-download-strong">v{{ beta_target }}</strong> will be the first public beta. Cross-platform: anywhere CPython runs.</p>
        <div class="ko-platform-tags">
          <span class="ko-platform-tag">Linux</span>
          <span class="ko-platform-tag">MacOS</span>
          <span class="ko-platform-tag">CPython 3.9+</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ko-download-cmds">
        <div class="ko-cmd-box">
          <div class="ko-cmd-label">PyPI &middot; weekly dev snapshot</div>
          <div class="ko-cmd-line"><span class="ko-cmd-prompt">$</span> pip install --pre koskari</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ko-cmd-box">
          <div class="ko-cmd-label">From source</div>
          <div class="ko-cmd-line"><span class="ko-cmd-prompt">$</span> git clone {{ repo_short }}</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- footer -->
  <div class="ko-footer">
    <div class="ko-footer-brand">
      <img src="koskari-icon.svg" alt="" width="26" height="26">
      <span class="ko-footer-name">Koskari</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ko-footer-meta">{{ license_label }} &middot; <span class="ko-footer-end"># The end.</span></div>
  </div>

</div>
</body>
</html>
